    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description xmlns:xmpMM="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/mm/" rdf:about="">
      <xmpMM:DocumentID>uuid:c80f4b7c-1c32-4e79-abdf-f54500b9760f</xmpMM:DocumentID>
      <xmpMM:InstanceID>urn:uuid:F6C0963F-1855-4EB0-9E62-A442EC783196</xmpMM:InstanceID>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description xmlns:xmpRights="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/rights/" rdf:about="">
      <xmpRights:Marked>True</xmpRights:Marked>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description xmlns:photoshop="http://ns.adobe.com/photoshop/1.0/" rdf:about="">
      <photoshop:AuthorsPosition>Mukhopadhyay</photoshop:AuthorsPosition>
      <photoshop:CaptionWriter>Dr. Raghupati Mukhopadhyay obtained his B.Sc. (Hons.) in Chemistry from University of Calcutta and M.Tech. with first class from University Colleges of Science &amp; Technology, Calcutta University in 1968. He joined as senior Research Fellow of C.S.I.R in the Deptt. of Applied Chemistry Calcutta University, in the year 1969. He obtained his Ph.D in Chemistry in 1977, and joined Dey-se-Chem. Ltd. as Chief Chemist. He joined Raja Peary Mohan College, Hooghly, West Bengal as a Reader in Chemistry in 1982 and as guest lecturer in the Deptt. of Chemical Technology, Calcutta University in the same year. He has guided many research projects both of fundamental and industrial nature. He has published more than ten research papers in reputed national journals and authored more than twelve books. He is a Fellow of Indian Chemical Society. He is also a Fellow of All India Institute of Chemists and has recently been selected as a Council Member of the same Institute.</photoshop:CaptionWriter>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description xmlns:pdf="http://ns.adobe.com/pdf/1.3/" rdf:about="">
      <pdf:Keywords>The book is meant for students of engineering degree colleges all over India. The syllabi covers various topics on physical chemistry; organic chemistry; industrial chemistry; and inorganic chemistry. To cover a variety of topics in a single book; that too for beginners; is a very difficult task. We have tried to present the subject matter very lucidly so that the students can grasp it easily. Some portions of the subject matter have been highlighted so that the students can understand the important and salient features of the topics. The book covers the latest syllabi of West Bengal State Council of Technical Education. Short questions and answers are given in the book for the benefit of the students for semester exams.</pdf:Keywords>
      <pdf:Producer>3-Heights(TM) PDF Security Shell 4.5.24.1 (http://www.pdf-tools.com)</pdf:Producer>
      <pdf:PDFVersion>1.7</pdf:PDFVersion>
    </rdf:Description>
  </rdf:RDF>
